From: Jim Harris <jim.harris@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: honor negotiated I/O pages for explicit buffered reads

Backport upstream 98b4ca2378e1f6b6c06a74f699623ebecfb3549d to 6.18.44:
https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=98b4ca2378e1f6b6c06a74f699623ebecfb3549d

The guest requests one MiB at a time and our VirtioFS backend negotiates
256 pages, but the FUSE backing device leaves io_pages at its default.
Large reads therefore split into 128-KiB round trips. A 352-MB prepared
image generated about 2,700 FUSE_READ requests and spent 1.5 seconds in
read(), while its BLAKE3 hash took only 76 ms.

Set the optimal I/O pages to the negotiated maximum for every FUSE mount.
This increases only explicitly requested reads above the read-ahead window;
speculative read-ahead and small/random reads retain their existing bounds.
It also applies to workspace I/O and retained mounts after warm resume.
Remove the backport when the pinned kernel carries the upstream change.

---
 fs/fuse/inode.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/fuse/inode.c b/fs/fuse/inode.c
--- a/fs/fuse/inode.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/inode.c
@@ -1463,6 +1463,7 @@ static void process_init_reply(struct fuse_mount *fm, struct fuse_args *args,
 
 		fm->sb->s_bdi->ra_pages =
 				min(fm->sb->s_bdi->ra_pages, ra_pages);
+		fm->sb->s_bdi->io_pages = fc->max_pages;
 		fc->minor = arg->minor;
 		fc->max_write = arg->minor < 5 ? 4096 : arg->max_write;
 		fc->max_write = max_t(unsigned, 4096, fc->max_write);
